Notwithstanding any other provision of this division, the governing body shall be authorized, by a majority vote, to waive the solicitation of bids for any purchases of used equipment in amounts not exceeding $50,000.00 if the following requirements with respect to such proposed purchase are met:
(1) The equipment to be purchased is used;
(2) The equipment to be purchased is in such condition that it may be, upon delivery, immediately put in operation by the county department to which such equipment is assigned without substantial repairs;
(3) The used equipment must be either offered for sale directly by another governmental entity, by or through an online bid site used primarily by governmental entities for the sale of used equipment, or from a private vendor;
(4) It must be verified prior to approval of the purchase that the purchase price is consistent with current market prices of similar used equipment as established by recent sales, published valuations, and other verifiable sources of price information;
(5) There must be a determination by the board of commissioners that there is an immediate necessity for the purchase of such equipment so that requiring normal bid processes would potentially jeopardize the public health or safety;
(6) The purchase price of the used equipment does not exceed $50,000.00.
No purchase of used equipment shall be divided into its component parts in an attempt to meet the $50,000.00 purchase price limit under this section.
Notwithstanding any other provision of this section, no purchase of used equipment shall be authorized unless funds for such purchase have been appropriated in the current annual county budget.
(Ord. of 11-12-2013(1))
